 gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-voverlay,
 gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-vsplit,
 gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-vtransform,
Description: Complete collection of Qualcomm GStreamer plugins for multimedia and ML processing
 This metapackage installs all Qualcomm GStreamer plugins, providing comprehensive
 support for video processing, machine learning inference, metadata handling,
 messaging, and inter-process communication. Designed for Qualcomm platforms,
 these plugins enable efficient multimedia pipelines with hardware acceleration
 and AI capabilities.

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-batch
Section: libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: GStreamer plugin for batching multiple stream buffers
 Provides the qtibatch element for batching buffers from multiple input streams
 into a single output buffer. Useful for efficient processing of multiple video
 or data streams simultaneously, reducing overhead in multi-stream scenarios.

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-metamux
Section: libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: GStreamer plugin for multiplexing video/audio streams with metadata
 Provides the qtimetamux element for muxing video or audio streams with metadata
 streams. Enables synchronization of media content with associated metadata such
 as detection results, classifications, or custom annotations in ML pipelines.

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-metatransform
Section: libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: GStreamer plugin for metadata processing and transformation
 Provides the qtimetatransform element for processing, filtering, and converting
 metadata attached to buffers. Supports transformation of detection boxes,
 classification results, and other metadata formats between different coordinate
 systems and representations.

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-mlaclassification
Section: libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: GStreamer plugin for audio classification using machine learning
 Provides the qtimlaclassification element for performing audio classification
 inference. Processes audio streams through ML models to identify sounds, speech,
 or audio events. (Legacy plugin, consider using mlpostprocess instead)

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-mlaconverter
Section: libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: GStreamer plugin for audio-to-tensor conversion for ML inference
 Provides the qtimlaconverter element for converting audio streams into tensor
 format suitable for machine learning model input. Handles audio preprocessing
 including resampling, normalization, and feature extraction.

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-mldemux
Section: libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: GStreamer plugin for demultiplexing ML inference results
 Provides the qtimldemux element for demultiplexing and routing machine learning
 inference results. Separates batched ML outputs into individual streams for
 parallel post-processing or different downstream consumers.

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-mlmetaextractor
Section: libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: GStreamer plugin for extracting metadata from buffers
 Provides the qtimlmetaextractor element for extracting metadata attached to
 buffers and converting it to text or structured format. Useful for debugging,
 logging, or exporting ML inference results and annotations.

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-mlmetaparser
Section: libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: GStreamer plugin for parsing and attaching metadata to buffers
 Provides the qtimlmetaparser element for parsing text-based metadata and
 attaching it to GStreamer buffers. Enables injection of external annotations,
 ground truth data, or pre-computed results into media pipelines.

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-mlpostprocess
Section: libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: GStreamer plugin for ML inference post-processing
 Provides the qtimlpostprocess element for post-processing machine learning
 inference results. Supports multiple model types including object detection
 (YOLO, SSD, MobileNet), classification, segmentation, and pose estimation.
 Converts raw model outputs into structured metadata with bounding boxes,
 labels, and confidence scores.

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-mlvclassification
Section: libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: GStreamer plugin for video classification using machine learning
 Provides the qtimlvclassification element for performing video/image
 classification inference. Processes video frames through ML models to identify
 objects, scenes, or activities. (Legacy plugin, consider using mlpostprocess)

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-mlvconverter
Section: libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: GStreamer plugin for video-to-tensor conversion for ML inference
 Provides the qtimlvconverter element for converting video frames into tensor
 format suitable for machine learning model input. Supports various preprocessing
 operations including scaling, cropping, color space conversion, normalization,
 and ROI extraction for efficient batch processing.

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-mlvdetection
Section: libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: GStreamer plugin for object detection using machine learning
 Provides the qtimlvdetection element for performing object detection inference
 on video streams. Identifies and localizes objects in frames using ML models.
 (Legacy plugin, consider using mlpostprocess instead)

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-mlvpose
Section: libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: GStreamer plugin for pose estimation using machine learning
 Provides the qtimlvpose element for performing human pose estimation inference.
 Detects body keypoints and skeletal structure from video frames using ML models.
 (Legacy plugin, consider using mlpostprocess instead)

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-mlvsegmentation
Section: libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: GStreamer plugin for semantic segmentation using machine learning
 Provides the qtimlvsegmentation element for performing semantic or instance
 segmentation inference. Classifies each pixel in video frames into categories
 using ML models. (Legacy plugin, consider using mlpostprocess instead)

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-mlvsuperresolution
Section: libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: GStreamer plugin for video super-resolution using machine learning
 Provides the qtimlvsuperresolution element for enhancing video resolution using
 ML-based super-resolution models. Upscales low-resolution video to higher
 resolution with improved quality and detail preservation.

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-msgbroker
Section: libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: GStreamer plugin for message broker integration (MQTT, Kafka)
 Provides the qtimsgbroker element for publishing GStreamer pipeline events and
 metadata to message brokers. Supports MQTT, Apache Kafka Pub/Sub
 for integration with IoT platforms, analytics systems, and distributed
 applications.

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-objtracker
Section: libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: GStreamer plugin for multi-object tracking
 Provides the qtiobjtracker element for tracking detected objects across video
 frames. Assigns persistent IDs to objects and maintains tracking through
 occlusions and frame-to-frame variations using algorithms like IOU, KCF,
 or deep learning-based trackers.

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-redissink
Section: libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: GStreamer sink plugin for Redis database
 Provides the qtiredissink element for publishing GStreamer buffers and metadata
 to Redis database. Enables real-time data streaming to Redis for caching,
 pub/sub messaging, or integration with Redis-based applications.

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-restricted-zone
Section: libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: GStreamer plugin for restricted zone detection and monitoring
 Provides the qtirestrictedzone element for detecting when objects enter or
 exit predefined restricted zones in video frames. Useful for security
 applications, safety monitoring, and perimeter intrusion detection with
 configurable zone geometries and alert generation.

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-rtspbin
Section: libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: GStreamer bin plugin for RTSP streaming
 Provides the qtirtspbin element, a convenience bin for RTSP (Real-Time
 Streaming Protocol) server functionality. Simplifies creation of RTSP streaming
 pipelines with built-in session management, authentication, and multi-client
 support for IP camera and streaming applications.

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-socket
Section: libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: GStreamer plugins for Unix domain socket communication
 Provides qtisocketsrc and qtisocketsink elements for transferring GStreamer
 buffers between processes using Unix domain sockets. Enables zero-copy
 inter-process communication with support for video frames, tensors, metadata,
 and file descriptor passing for efficient pipeline distribution.

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-tools
Section: utils
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: Utility tools for Qualcomm GStreamer plugins
 Provides command-line utilities and helper tools for working with Qualcomm
 GStreamer plugins. Includes pipeline testing tools, performance profiling
 utilities, and debugging aids for development and troubleshooting.

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-uridecodebin
Section: libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: The plugin extends GStreamer's URI decoding capabilities by creating
 and managing decoding pipelines for multimedia streams obtained from
 URI sources.

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-vcomposer
Section: libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: GStreamer plugin for video composition and layout
 Provides the qtivcomposer element for compositing multiple video streams into
 a single output with configurable layouts. Supports picture-in-picture, split
 screen, grid layouts, and custom positioning with alpha blending and scaling
 for multi-view applications and video walls.

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-videotemplate
Section: libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: GStreamer plugin template for custom video processing
 Provides a template plugin (qtivideotemplate) demonstrating best practices
 for creating custom video processing elements. Serves as a starting point
 for developers building proprietary or specialized video processing plugins
 for Qualcomm platforms.

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-voverlay
Section: libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: GStreamer plugin for video overlay and graphics rendering
 Provides the qtivoverlay element for overlaying graphics, text, bounding boxes,
 and annotations on video frames. Supports Cairo-based rendering with
 anti-aliasing, transparency, and dynamic content updates for visualization
 of ML inference results, OSD (on-screen display), and UI elements.

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-vsplit
Section: libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: GStreamer plugin for video stream splitting and ROI extraction
 Provides the qtivsplit element for splitting video streams and extracting
 regions of interest (ROIs). Supports multiple output pads with independent
 cropping, scaling, and format conversion. Useful for multi-resolution encoding,
 ROI-based processing, and parallel ML inference on different image regions.

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-vtransform
Section: libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: GStreamer plugin for video transformation and format conversion
 Provides the qtivtransform element for video format conversion, scaling,
 cropping, and color space transformation. Leverages Qualcomm hardware
 accelerators for efficient video processing with support for
 various formats including NV12, NV21, RGBA, and compressed formats.

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-base
Section: libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: Base library for Qualcomm GStreamer plugins
 Provides common infrastructure, utilities, and base classes used by Qualcomm
 GStreamer plugins. Includes memory allocators, metadata definitions, ML
 framework integration, video utilities, and hardware abstraction layers.
 Required dependency for most Qualcomm GStreamer plugins.

Package: libgstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-base-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
  gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk-base (= ${binary:Version}),
  ${misc:Depends},
Description: Development files for Qualcomm GStreamer base library
 Provides headers, pkg-config files, and development libraries for building
 custom GStreamer plugins that integrate with Qualcomm's plugin ecosystem.
 Includes APIs for metadata handling, ML integration, hardware acceleration,
 and common utilities.

Package: gstreamer1.0-imsdk-python-examples
Section: utils
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 python3,
 python3-gst-1.0,
 python3-opencv,
 gstreamer1.0-plugins-imsdk,
Description: Python examples for Qualcomm GStreamer plugins
 Provides Python-based example applications and scripts demonstrating usage
 of Qualcomm GStreamer plugins through Python bindings. Includes examples for
 ML inference, video processing, metadata handling, and pipeline construction
 using PyGObject and OpenCV integration.

